# Payments Ecosystem Brief — November 2, 2026

## Macro picture

This week shows payment networks expanding in several directions:

- **Private platforms are becoming payment networks.** Stripe now lets businesses transfer funds directly to other Stripe businesses.
- **Domestic bank-payment systems are becoming internationally usable.** Malaysian customers can now use their banking apps at foreign Alipay+ QR merchants.
- **Authentication is moving away from one-time codes.** Visa passkeys have reached a live merchant rollout.
- **New public infrastructure remains years away.** The ECB has contracted the connectivity layer for a digital-euro pilot, but has not decided to issue a digital euro.

No similarly consequential new FedNow, RTP or ACH deployment was identified this week.

