## Longer-term watch: the digital euro’s connection layer

On **October 30**, the ECB announced two groups of network-service providers that will connect banks, payment providers and central banks to the proposed digital-euro platform:

- Nexi Payments and Deutsche Telekom Business Solutions.
- Telefónica de España, Telefónica Global Solutions and Indra.

The first contract is supporting the pilot; the second starts in **May 2027**. Both are expected to be capable of supporting potential issuance from **2029**, subject to a future ECB decision.

These companies would provide secure connectivity, similar to dedicated network access to a payment platform. They would not themselves issue the currency.

**Retail-banking implication:** The announcement makes the technical connection model more concrete for participating institutions, but it does not establish a consumer launch date.

**Status:** Pilot preparation. A retail digital euro is not live or finally approved.

**Source:** [ECB — Network service providers selected for the digital euro](https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/intro/news/html/ecb.mipnews261030.en.html)